# Accepted risks for the image scan in CI (trivy image --severity HIGH,CRITICAL
# --ignore-unfixed --ignorefile .trivyignore). One entry per vulnerability, each with why
# it is accepted and an exp: date, after which Trivy stops ignoring it and the build fails
# until somebody looks again. A vulnerability with a fix in a dependency is fixed, not
# listed here.

# pcre2 and pcre2-syntax 10.40-6.el9 in the runtime base image
# (ubi9/openjdk-21-runtime:1.24, built 2026-10-12, the newest there is). Fixed in
# 10.40-7.el9_8, which arrives when Red Hat rebuilds the base and Dependabot moves the
# pinned digest. PCRE2 is a library of the operating system's tools in the image; the
# application never calls it, and nothing from outside reaches it as a regular expression.
CVE-2026-103111 exp:2026-11-17
CVE-2026-86145 exp:2026-11-17
CVE-2026-89161 exp:2026-11-17

# krb5-libs 1.21.1-10.el9_8.1 in the runtime base image (ubi9/openjdk-21-runtime); fixed in
# 1.21.1-10.el9_9.2, which is not in the public UBI 9 BaseOS repository yet, so the Dockerfile's
# microdnf update cannot take it. Every one is in the KDC (krb5kdc) or the admin server (kadmind):
# the image has neither krb5-server nor any Kerberos daemon, only the client library the
# operating system's tools link, and the JVM does its own Kerberos. Remove these once UBI
# publishes el9_9.2.
CVE-2026-107364 exp:2026-12-15
CVE-2026-112315 exp:2026-12-15
CVE-2026-112316 exp:2026-12-15
CVE-2026-112317 exp:2026-12-15
CVE-2026-112318 exp:2026-12-15
CVE-2026-112319 exp:2026-12-15
CVE-2026-112320 exp:2026-12-15
CVE-2026-112321 exp:2026-12-15
CVE-2026-112322 exp:2026-12-15
CVE-2026-112323 exp:2026-12-15
CVE-2026-118380 exp:2026-12-15
CVE-2026-119079 exp:2026-12-15
CVE-2026-71199 exp:2026-12-15
CVE-2026-71200 exp:2026-12-15
